{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/514389-cross-covenant-benefits-merits-oaths-laws-coils-scales-cr\u00faac-theban-sorceries","id":514389,"title":"Cross-covenant benefits: Merits, Oaths, Laws, Coils/Scales, Cr\u00faac, Theban Sorceries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-14T12:34:01-07:00","id":514389,"title":"Cross-covenant benefits: Merits, Oaths, Laws, Coils/Scales, Cr\u00faac, Theban Sorceries","content":"Hi !<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I understand the rules for Covenants properly, especially when you start to mix things up.<br /> <br /> So, a starting character needs to purchase Status ([Covenant]) 1 to start gaining benefits as par \u00abCovenants offer certain advantages to their members. In order to purchase these advantages, your character must have at least one dot in the Covenant Status Merit\u00bb (p.80)<br /> <br /> Within the bounds of not having more than five dots total of Covenant Status, can you mix and match as you want? The rules talk about &quot;affiliated group&quot; and &quot;group to which she belongs&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR, p.113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character could theoretically gain Status within multiple covenants. Most of the covenants will allow members to dabble in other organizations, so long as they don\u2019t share secrets. The Ordo Dracul, for example, will not stop a member from attending Sanctified mass. But the moment she shares her knowledge of the Coils, she\u2019ll find her Requiem cut abruptly short. Her combined dots in one type of Status (City, Clan, or Covenant) cannot exceed five, and she may never have as many dots in her affiliated group as she does to the group to which she belongs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... can I be a Ordo Dracul 3, Invictus 2 member? What about Ordo Dracul 2, Invictus 1, Circle of the Crone 1, Lancea et Sanctum 1 ? Is it possible, theoretically, to have one dot in each of the five covenants, or is it forbidden as per the aforementioned quote?<br /> <br /> Depending on the legality of the above, could someone thus learn Oaths, Laws, Coils/Scales, Cr\u00faac, and Theban Sorceries?<br /> <br /> As long as one doesn't &quot;share secrets&quot;, it seems one could keep all merits (and Coils/Cr\u00faac/Theban Sorceries, I'd guess), given that \u00abIf the character changes or abandons their covenant, the Merit does not go away\u00bb (p.109).<br /> <br /> The whole point of my question is that I'm making a city Prince, and I want him to be both Invictus (primarily) and Ordo Dracul (secondarily). I also want my players to know their options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:05:37-07:00","id":514451,"title":"","content":"Ordo Dracul 3 and Invictus 2 is fine. Circle of the Crone and Lancea et Sanctum seems a bit weird. Technically, you can't get all five unless you are a Carthian with Right of Return p.116. You have to pick a main convenant which must have 2 before you can pick up others. That limits you to 3 covenants with 1 aside from the main one you chose. You could switch your main within reason, but you might lose status in other covenants to make it work out. It would be easier to get status with a covenant, learn what you want and leave if you want some of everything. The Prince needs to have at least one more dot in Invictus than Ordo Dracul, so 3:2 is your max.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T15:21:49-07:00","id":514543,"title":"","content":"That's the fiddly side of things. Narratively, good luck explaining how a character can survive amidst a tangled web of loyalty and educations and threats from the different Covenants they're obligated to work for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:11:32-07:00","id":514597,"title":"","content":"Obviously, the byzantine / labyrinthine mess of tangled webs would be a hell to socially manage. I'm not advocating &quot;playing&quot; one who has her/his fingers in FOUR covenants at once (2/1/1/1), but I still needed to know the limit.<br /> <br /> So basically, you're all saying once could conceivably amass Oaths, Laws, Coils/Scales, Cr\u00faac, <i>and </i>Theban Sorceries (if one switches one covenant to another and gets to keep his/her Merits from back then).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:11:39-07:00","id":514599,"title":"","content":"You should probably figure out the dynamics between the Covenants. Invictus and Carthians are usually against each other. The Circle and Lance are against each other. The Ordo Dracul might have problems with the Circle, depends on the cult, or the Lance, depending on the school of thought the Dragons are working under. If you are working with Covenants at least nominally being enemies then don't allow status in both at the same time. It would take an exceptional individual to have status in enemy camps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:19:54-07:00","id":514602,"title":"","content":"The question of social feasibility is kind of mitigated by... well... immortality. And by that I mean that a very <i>very </i>Old vampire could have had &quot;phases&quot;. In theory, once could have even retained Roman Camarilla Merits (not that they would do much good...), or at least be a former Camarilla member. One could have been a devout &quot;Catholic&quot; L+S member before the Lutheran Reform, or before Industrialization, etc. Given enough time, which there's no shortage of with Immortality, one could have legitimately have switched allegiance without the &quot;switch&quot; being so much a <i>Betrayal</i> as the effect of broader social changes.<br /> <br /> I have this 400-450 years old Dacian (from the Carpathian Mt.) Vampire in mind, she could have been exposed to Theban Sorcery or Cr\u00faac long ago, and left. She would retain what she learned and could live on a whole different continent without many people knowing, and the rare few that would could reasonably be interesting old enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:26:08-07:00","id":514606,"title":"","content":"Would you really have covenant status if no one in the covenant knows you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:28:14-07:00","id":514608,"title":"","content":"Yes, but in those cases the covenant status would have been lost long ago, so you would just make a note in their history and buy as if they had the status at the time. That means no future leaning of secrets. There are actually published characters that are built like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:11:03-07:00","id":515098,"title":"","content":"In theory, you could pull it off. Realistically, you'd become a hunted person as you piss off your covenants. No one would accept someone renowned for continually jumping ship. No Accolyte would teach deep mysteries of Cruac, nor the advanced Sanctified Theban mysteries, to someone so dedicated to the cause. A lot of Carthian Law effects rely on Carthian status. Invictus Oaths tend to require being sworn to others, giving obvious fealty to another, and following their orders. <br /> <br /> The thing with vampire is that, while mechanically you can do a lot of things, the consequences are almost always social. Which makes sense - Vampire is a primarily social game. You have to keep that in mind whenever you try to do something. Mostly, books won't say specifically &quot;You can't have Invictus and Carthian status at once!&quot; because in some games, the Estate and Movement are allies. But its something that you have to keep in mind in individual settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T13:37:35-07:00","id":515410,"title":"","content":"Based on what I've read about the Ordo Dracul, seems like it would be exceedingly difficult to be one of the Sworn and have enough time to maintain sincere ties to other covenants (though being an Academy-approved mole in another covenant is another matter entirely). I think you could dip your toes enough to get instruction in the Coils while having simultaneous membership in other groups, but once you've taken an oath you have enough responsibilities and oversight that divided loyalties would probably result in you having one of those &quot;chrysalis accidents&quot; that require a draugr to be destroyed for the good of all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}